{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c387","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adf6-85aa-70c2-bc58-c12e2d2660fd"},"sequence":30,"recorded_at":1780531400000055,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"fd38f806-c210-492a-8285-9e843f4a64a5","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"fd38f806-c210-492a-8285-9e843f4a64a5","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"fd38f806-c210-492a-8285-9e843f4a64a5"},"call_id":"call_01a0adf698407128a4b025b0da0bf5d3","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-1-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board m 'set_status(TASK-260917-3lt2xv, status=development)' 2>&1 | head -20; echo \\\"---\\\"; cat /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260917-3lt2xv/TASK-260917-3lt2xv_producer.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Set status and read producer instructions\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"primary\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"status_changed\\\",\\\"element_id\\\":\\\"TASK-260917-3lt2xv\\\",\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"new_value\\\":\\\"development\\\",\\\"old_value\\\":\\\"to-dev\\\"},\\\"side_effects\\\":[{\\\"action\\\":\\\"promoted\\\",\\\"element_id\\\":\\\"STORY-260917-158jyi\\\",\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"new_value\\\":\\\"development\\\",\\\"old_value\\\":\\\"to-dev\\\"},{\\\"action\\\":\\\"escalated\\\",\\\"element_id\\\":\\\"EPIC-260916-18uelk\\\",\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"new_value\\\":\\\"development\\\",\\\"old_value\\\":\\\"integrating\\\"}]}}\\n---\\nOwn TASK-260917-3lt2xv (make-cataloggen-check-release-agnostic), the single leaf of STORY-260917-158jyi (release-agnostic-catalog-validation-gate) under EPIC-260916-18uelk. Why: Change Request construction runs the CONTROL ROOT's configured validation suite against a candidate; validation command 21 is today `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -metadata internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json -contracts internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check`, so a Story that re-points the catalog to a newly pinned revision (TASK-260916-n9r71p for v0.7.0 right now; CR-TASK-260916-n9r71p-1 failed at command 21 with \\\"normative source pin mismatch: source identity drift\\\"; the v0.6.0 adoption hit the same collision, see TASK-260908-2tkufa_integration-outcome.md) can never pass construction, because its own cataloggen correctly refuses the stale lock. Fix the contract at the source, not with a workaround: (1) declare the adopted release once in internal/catalog (for example `const Adopted Release = ReleaseV060` next to Current(), with Current() defined through it so the two cannot diverge; add a test pinning Current().Release == Adopted); (2) add an `-adopted` mode to internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen that derives `-metadata internal/catalog/catalog.<adopted>.json` and `-contracts internal/specpin/<adopted>.lock.json` from catalog.Adopted relative to a `-root` (default \\\".\\\" — the validation suite runs from the repository root), refuses `-adopted` combined with explicit -metadata/-contracts, refuses a missing metadata or lock file with distinct messages naming the derived path, refuses a lock whose source release differs from the adopted release before generation, and otherwise behaves byte-identically to the explicit invocation (same Generate call, same -check/-output semantics); (3) switch validation command 21 in task-board.config.json to `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` (edit exactly that string in the candidate; never edit the control root; every other command unchanged) and prove it green on the candidate; (4) README tool row for cataloggen documents the -adopted form and the explicit form; LOGBOOK entry. No catalog content, metadata, lock or generated-output change: `git diff --exit-code internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json internal/specpin/` must be empty. Tests drive the production entry (the cataloggen run function / main through os/exec) with positives (-adopted -check green; -adopted generation byte-identical to explicit generation into a temp output; explicit flags still work) and refusals (mixed flags; missing metadata; missing lock; lock release != adopted via a temp root with a v0.5.0 lock copied under the adopted name; stale generated output under -adopted -check), a narrowing mutant per refusal and per the byte-identity claim with a shipped harness (per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, an applied harmless SURVIVED control), and a conformance row map to the task AC. Managed Story worktree contract: the worktree is provisioned by task-board under .temp/STORY-260917-158jyi/worktree on branch task-board/story/STORY-260917-158jyi forked from current trunk; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED, never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept; if origin/main moves before your handoff, run task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260917-3lt2xv and restore any trunk-changed path the refresh left stale with a single-path git checkout HEAD -- <path>; before handoff verify git status shows only candidate paths (no __pycache__, no .pyc). This is the Story's only leaf, so the CR is story_final. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local; run the full configured validation suite once before the handoff (your candidate's command 21 and trunk's explicit command 21 must BOTH be green on your tree — construction will run trunk's); hand off no later than 1.5 hours in. Attach TASK-260917-3lt2xv_results.md, TASK-260917-3lt2xv_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260917-3lt2xv_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then task-board handoff TASK-260917-3lt2xv --role developer and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be muse-spark xhigh while codex is out of quota.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4860,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1215,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
