nd Observation Events, validate the Structured Error registry, its static containing-contract bindings, and its detail redaction, validate the CLI Result envelopes, command bodies, common flags, rendering boundary, and exit-status mapping, classify one completed `ax --json` invocation from stdout and its exit status through the machine reader and replay the frozen historical envelope corpora, generate and check the typed catalogs, build, test, and measure the Go implementation | `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck`; `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck -section 6.2` (every other assigned section is refused with its measured coverage ratio); `go test ./internal/config -cover -count=1`; `go test ./internal/localstore -cover -count=1`; `go test ./internal/scalar -cover -count=1`; `go test ./internal/scalar -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzScalarProductionEntries$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1`; `go test ./internal/canonicaljson -cover -count=1`; `go test ./internal/axerror -cover -count=1`; `go test ./internal/cliresult -cover -count=1`; `go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzCanonicalizeRoundTrip$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1`; `go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzObjectIdentityRepresentationInvariant$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1`; `go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzClosedIdentityShapeRefusal$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1`; `go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzObservationEventRefusal$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1`; `go generate ./internal/catalog`; `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -metadata internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json -contracts internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check`; `go test ./... -v`; `go test ./... -cover`; `go build ./...` | Read-only traceability report; owner-only roots, immutable blob/quarantine data, and `<state>/index.sqlite` plus recovery evidence only when storage entries are called; `internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go`; Go build/fuzz cache; test output captured under `.temp/<TASK-ID>/` when needed |\\nLOGBOOK.md:318:- RECOVERY: prior CR1 failed command 21 because task-board.config.json still passed v0.5.0 inputs to the strict v0.6.0 generator. Changed only that command in candidate and authorized control root; control-root pre-existing config diff was empty and both complete config files now match. TestConfiguredCRCatalogGateConsumesAdoptedAuthority drives the configured command through cataloggen.run and refuses stale authority. No model, signing, required gate or hosted-trigger policy changed.\\nLOGBOOK.md:398:- CARRIED (pre-existing, fixed here): `//go:generate` → `// go:generate` disarmed the generator while the token survived and the freshness diff stayed clean (reproduced: old step exits 0 on the rewrite). Fix: anchored `grep -c '^//go:generate'` pin in the freshness step + committed `TestGenerateDirectiveStaysRecognizedForm`; the rewrite now fails the guard (exit 1) and the pin while catalog/cataloggen stay otherwise green (battery G-directive-space, behavioral suite executed).\\nLOGBOOK.md:950:- ROOT CAUSE: **a clause was claimed against a topically related section instead of against the actor its MUST binds.** Ownership clause `15.1#6` at SPEC.md:11047 was discharged by `LocalFromUntrusted`. That line's only RFC 2119 sentence is \\\"The plugin MUST NOT masquerade a different-major object as v2\\\" - it binds the **provider plugin**, a child process this repository does not build; its only binaries are `cataloggen` and `tracecheck`. The host half of the same table row, which `LocalFromUntrusted` does implement, carries no RFC 2119 keyword at all, so it is not what the clause scanner measured.\\nLOGBOOK.md:1029:- EVIDENCE: `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck -section 15.2` exited **0**. §15.2 is the nineteen-row normative exit-code registry (SPEC.md:11073-11095) and nothing in the tree implements it — the only `os.Exit` calls are the `exit(1)` paths of `cataloggen` and `tracecheck`. Same for `-section 7.3`, the closed Provider Manifest, whose sole trace is a catalog row naming its URN. Both were bound to `internal/catalog/catalog.go:ForRelease`, an unrelated symbol.\\nLOGBOOK.md:1119:- STATUS: `internal/canonicaljson` 97.2% before and after, verified against a `git archive HEAD` baseline. gofmt, `go build ./...`, both cross-compile targets, `go vet ./...`, `go test ./... -count=1`, `-cover -count=1`, `-race -count=1`, tracecheck, `cataloggen -check` and all five fuzz gates at 100x exit 0.\\nLOGBOOK.md:1131:- STATUS: `internal/localstore` unchanged at 86.6%, 90 top-level tests and 130 subtests — this round added assertions to existing cases, not new cases. gofmt, `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `go test ./... -count=1`, `-race -count=1`, `-cover -count=1`, both cross-compile targets, global tracecheck, `cataloggen -check` and `git diff --check` all exit 0.\\nAGENTS.md\\nCLAUDE.md\\nLOGBOOK.md\\nREADME.md\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 8952,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2238,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
