{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c539","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adf6-85aa-70c2-bc58-c12e2d2660fd"},"sequence":247,"recorded_at":1780531400000489,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"fd38f806-c210-492a-8285-9e843f4a64a5","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"fd38f806-c210-492a-8285-9e843f4a64a5","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"fd38f806-c210-492a-8285-9e843f4a64a5"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0adf7-0f20-7472-9507-6eafcdddb886"},"task_id":"01a0adf7-0f20-7472-9507-6eafcdddb886","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0adf7-0f20-7472-9507-6eafcdddb886","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(2569 line(s) above)\n2570|| Release projection | Contracts | Operations | Capability names | Events | Error codes |\n2571|| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n2572|| v0.5.0 | 60 | 99 | 46 | 112 | 109 |\n2573|| v0.4.3 | 55 | 89 | 30 | 112 | 94 |\n2574|\n2575|The source pin and catalog metadata cover every normative top-level section\n2576|claimed by the implementation board: Sections 1-20 and Appendices A-D. Each\n2577|generated family retains its exact defining section and named\n2578|Appendix D fixture anchors. Durable operation entries include\n2579|their reviewed idempotency scope and crash/lost-result recovery evidence;\n2580|Terminal Backend entries reproduce the distinct Section 4.C canonical keys.\n2581|Capability entries are vocabulary members only: the public type has no\n2582|availability, enabled, supported, or status field, so catalog generation cannot\n2583|advertise runtime capability.\n2584|\n2585|Regenerate and verify the committed output with:\n2586|\n2587|```bash\n2588|go generate ./internal/catalog\n2589|go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -metadata internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json -contracts internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\n2590|go test ./internal/catalog ./internal/cataloggen ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -count=1\n2591|```\n2592|\n2593|## Specification-to-Code Ownership Gate\n2594|\n2595|[`internal/traceability`](internal/traceability) provides the read-only\n2596|repository gate used by CI. Its reviewed\n2597|[`ownership.v0.6.0.json`](internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json)\n2598|registry independently enumerates implementation owners for all 63 current\n2599|contract rows, 36 pinned or catalog-referenced normative section keys, 101\n2600|executable acceptance cases, 56 exact section bindings with their declared\n2601|coverage, 12 disclosed unowned sections, and 32 exact fixture identities or\n2602|Appendix D anchors. The v0.4.3 projection is checked as an owned 55-contract subset,\n2603|and the superseded v0.5.0 registry is checked as an owned legacy projection.\n2604|The generated v0.6.0 catalog also carries the reviewed schema/version/self-field\n2605|contracts used by canonical object identity calculation; generator validation\n2606|binds each row to a pinned contract and rejects duplicate, unsupported,\n2607|malformed, or digest-drifted metadata.\n2608|\n2609|The production validator re-verifies the exact source lock and reviewed catalog\n2610|metadata, refuses stale generated output, requires every production and test\n2611|owner to resolve to a real Go declaration, and rejects gaps, duplicates,\n2612|self-minted keys, partial or malformed reads, and semantic ownership drift.\n2613|GitHub Actions invokes the gate directly before generation, tests, vet, and\n2614|build:\n2615|\n2616|```bash\n2617|go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck\n2618|go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck -section 6.2\n2619|```\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
