lity`](internal/traceability) provides the read-only\n2596|repository gate used by CI. Its reviewed\n2597|[`ownership.v0.6.0.json`](internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json)\n2598|registry independently enumerates implementation owners for all 63 current\n2599|contract rows, 36 pinned or catalog-referenced normative section keys, 101\n2600|executable acceptance cases, 56 exact section bindings with their declared\n2601|coverage, 12 disclosed unowned sections, and 32 exact fixture identities or\n2602|Appendix D anchors. The v0.4.3 projection is checked as an owned 55-contract subset,\n2603|and the superseded v0.5.0 registry is checked as an owned legacy projection.\n2604|The generated v0.6.0 catalog also carries the reviewed schema/version/self-field\n2605|contracts used by canonical object identity calculation; generator validation\n2606|binds each row to a pinned contract and rejects duplicate, unsupported,\n2607|malformed, or digest-drifted metadata.\n2608|\n2609|The production validator re-verifies the exact source lock and reviewed catalog\n2610|metadata, refuses stale generated output, requires every production and test\n2611|owner to resolve to a real Go declaration, and rejects gaps, duplicates,\n2612|self-minted keys, partial or malformed reads, and semantic ownership drift.\n2613|GitHub Actions invokes the gate directly before generation, tests, vet, and\n2614|build:\n2615|\n2616|```bash\n2617|go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck\n2618|go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck -section 6.2\n2619|```\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
