{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c581","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adf6-85aa-70c2-bc58-c12e2d2660fd"},"sequence":283,"recorded_at":1780531400000561,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"fd38f806-c210-492a-8285-9e843f4a64a5","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"fd38f806-c210-492a-8285-9e843f4a64a5","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"fd38f806-c210-492a-8285-9e843f4a64a5"},"call_id":"call_01a0adf7148173eb9d7cad89a0fc2162","text":"Read text file `internal/specpin/pin.go`.\n(149 line(s) above)\n150|\treturn bytes.Clone(embeddedPinV060)\n151|}\n152|\n153|// Current returns a newly decoded copy of the embedded, verified release pin.\n154|//\n155|// Current still serves the v0.5.0 baseline: the platform-path registry in\n156|// internal/localstore binds that historical source explicitly through\n157|// CurrentV050. Catalogue, traceability, and CI gates consume the adopted\n158|// v0.6.0 authority through CurrentV060 instead.\n159|func Current() (Manifest, error) {\n160|\treturn Verify(embeddedPin)\n161|}\n162|\n163|// CurrentV050 is the explicit historical v0.5.0 baseline reader. It is the\n164|// binding intentionally-historical consumers declare, so a future change to\n165|// what Current serves cannot silently re-point them at a newer authority.\n166|func CurrentV050() (Manifest, error) {\n167|\treturn Verify(embeddedPin)\n168|}\n169|\n170|// CurrentV060 returns a newly decoded copy of the embedded, verified v0.6.0\n171|// release pin: the adopted normative source authority.\n172|func CurrentV060() (Manifest, error) {\n173|\treturn VerifyV060(embeddedPinV060)\n174|}\n175|\n176|func decode(candidate []byte) (Manifest, error) {\n177|\tvar manifest Manifest\n178|\tdecoder := json.NewDecoder(bytes.NewReader(candidate))\n179|\tdecoder.DisallowUnknownFields()\n180|\tif err := decoder.Decode(&manifest); err != nil {\n181|\t\treturn Manifest{}, mismatch(\"decode pin: %v\", err)\n182|\t}\n183|\n184|\tvar trailing any\n185|\tif err := decoder.Decode(&trailing); !errors.Is(err, io.EOF) {\n186|\t\tif err == nil {\n187|\t\t\treturn Manifest{}, mismatch(\"multiple JSON values\")\n188|\t\t}\n189|\t\treturn Manifest{}, mismatch(\"trailing JSON: %v\", err)\n190|\t}\n191|\treturn manifest, nil\n192|}\n193|\n194|// Verify accepts only the exact embedded release lock. It distinguishes a\n195|// failed or partial read from absence by returning ErrPinMismatch.\n196|func Verify(candidate []byte) (Manifest, error) {\n197|\tmanifest, err := decode(candidate)\n198|\tif err != nil {\n199|\t\treturn Manifest{}, err\n200|\t}\n201|\n202|\tif err := validate(manifest); err != nil {\n203|\t\treturn Manifest{}, err\n204|\t}\n205|\n206|\tdigest := sha256.Sum256(candidate)\n207|\tif hex.EncodeToString(digest[:]) != ManifestSHA256 {\n208|\t\treturn Manifest{}, mismatch(\"lock digest is not %s\", ManifestSHA256)\n209|\t}\n210|\n211|\treturn manifest, nil\n212|}\n213|\n214|// VerifyV060 accepts only the exact embedded v0.6.0 release lock. The v0.5.0\n215|// lock, a partial read, and any drifted or substituted pin are refused with\n216|// ErrPinMismatch, exactly as Verify refuses everything but the v0.5.0 bytes.\n217|func VerifyV060(candidate []byte) (Manifest, error) {\n218|\tmanifest, err := decode(candidate)\n219|\tif err != nil {\n220|\t\treturn Manifest{}, err\n221|\t}\n222|\n223|\tif err := validateV060(manifest); err != nil {\n224|\t\treturn Manifest{}, err\n225|\t}\n226|\n227|\tdigest := sha256.Sum256(candidate)\n228|\tif hex.EncodeToString(digest[:]) != ManifestSHA256V060 {\n229|\t\treturn Manifest{}, mismatch(\"lock digest is not %s\", ManifestSHA256V060)\n230|\t}\n231|\n232|\treturn manifest, nil\n233|}\n234|\n235|// ContractsForRelease returns an isolated ordered contract registry for one\n236|// of the releases explicitly represented by this pin.\n237|//\n238|// A v0.5.0 manifest represents v0.5.0 and v0.4.3, exactly as before: asking\n239|// it for v0.6.0 is refused, because a stale pin cannot authorize a release\n240|// it predates. A v0.6.0 manifest represents v0.6.0, and derives the exact\n241|// historical v0.5.0 and v0.4.3 registries without rewriting them: the v0.5.0\n242|// projection drops the three v0.6.0 rows and trims the four widened version\n243|// lists, which the cross-version test proves byte-equal to the real v0.5.0\n244|// lock.\n245|func (manifest Manifest) ContractsForRelease(release string) ([]ContractPin, error) {\n246|\tswitch release {\n247|\tcase ReleaseV060:\n248|\t\tif manifest.Source.Release != ReleaseV060 {\n249|\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: %s\", ErrUnsupportedRelease, release)\n250|\t\t}\n251|\t\treturn cloneContracts(manifest.Contracts), nil\n252|\tcase ReleaseV050:\n253|\t\tif manifest.Source.Release == ReleaseV060 {\n254|\t\t\treturn derivedV050Contracts(manifest)\n255|\t\t}\n256|\t\treturn cloneContracts(manifest.Contracts), nil\n257|\tcase ReleaseV043:\n258|\t\tabsent := make(map[string]struct{}, len(manifest.Compatibility.AbsentContracts))\n259|\t\tfor _, name := range manifest.Compatibility.AbsentContracts {\n260|\t\t\tabsent[name] = struct{}{}\n261|\t\t}\n262|\n263|\t\toverrides := make(map[string]ContractPin, len(manifest.Compatibility.VersionOverrides))\n264|\t\tfor _, contract := range manifest.Compatibility.VersionOverrides {\n265|\t\t\toverrides[contractKey(contract)] = contract\n266|\t\t}\n267|\n268|\t\tcontracts := make([]ContractPin, 0, len(manifest.Contracts)-len(absent))\n269|\t\tfor _, contract := range manifest.Contracts {\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c583","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adf6-85aa-70c2-bc58-c12e2d2660fd"},"sequence":284,"recorded_at":1780531400000563,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"fd38f806-c210-492a-8285-9e843f4a64a5","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"fd38f806-c210-492a-8285-9e843f4a64a5","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"fd38f806-c210-492a-8285-9e843f4a64a5"},"call_id":"call_01a0adf7162570188c331b5a09f97921","text":"Read text file `LOGBOOK.md`.\n1|# Flight Logbook\n2|\n3|> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n4|> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n5|\n6|## 2026-09-17\n7|\n8|### TASK-260830-21gygk — rev16 rework: normalize Go aliases in the sealed-capability census\n9|- REVIEW FINDING CLOSED (CR15 P2-A): the package-wide `go/types` census\n10|  compared lexical `*types.TypeName` objects, so a Go alias could bypass the\n11|  sealed `checkpointSeal`/`checkpointSealToken` inventory. The initial alias\n12|  baseline admitted the direct, token, chained, and container plants; its\n13|  recorded exit was 1 before the fix.\n14|- FIX (`internal/sessquery/rev11_regression_test.go`): every sealed type and\n15|  value identity path now applies `types.Unalias` before canonical comparison\n16|  and before structural descent. The recursive coverage includes chained\n17|  aliases, pointers, arrays, slices, maps, channels, structs, function\n18|  signatures, generic arguments, interfaces, type parameters, and unions.\n19|  Unrelated named capability types are not opened through their underlying\n20|  representation, so the census keeps the public capability boundary intact.\n21|- TESTS (`internal/sessquery/rev15_regression_test.go`): direct, chained,\n22|  container, and function-signature alias plants all refuse through the same\n23|  production census entry. The existing callback-provenance negative now binds\n24|  its unknown callback locally inside the approved profile flow, isolating the\n25|  callback object-identity gate from the independent package-scope sealed-value\n26|  guard; its narrowing mutant is killed by the same instrument.\n27|- MUTANTS: the final local battery (`mutants-rev16b`) reports 66/66 applied N/B\n28|  plants killed (63 narrowing, 3 ordering). The applied harmless control is\n29|  `SURVIVED`; `NOT_APPLIED` and `COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE` remain separate\n30|  classifier outcomes. The alias mutant removes `types.Unalias` only from the\n31|  nested sealed-value recursion path and fails the container plant.\n32|- CLEANUP: removed the stray `internal/sessquery/testdata/__pycache__` Python\n33|  cache from the candidate; the mutation copy restored all mutated source\n34|  bytes and the final candidate contains no Python cache artifact.\n35|- COVERAGE: 8 of 8 shared-library AC rows remain driven by named production\n36|  entries; public CLI/lifecycle coverage is 0 of 8 by the stated ownership\n37|  bound. These reads and revalidations perform no durable writes, so crash and\n38|  mutation-idempotency evidence is not applicable to this leaf.\n39|- HANDOFF: final validation logs, conformance/relation matrices, and the raw\n40|  mutation evidence are attached to this task for independent review. The\n41|  Story candidate remains uncommitted.\n42|\n43|### TASK-260830-21gygk — rev15 rework: close seal/token path and callback provenance census gaps\n44|- REVIEW FINDINGS CLOSED (CR14 P2): the package-wide `go/types` census no\n45|  longer relies on composite literals alone. It rejects `new(T)`, generic\n46|  constructors, explicit field mutation, interface copies, `reflect.TypeFor`,\n47|  and `unsafe.Pointer` paths by exact `checkpointSeal`/\n48|  `checkpointSealToken` object identity. Profile result calls accept only the\n49|  exact callback parameter object recorded for that profile entry; package\n50|  callback variables and struct-field callbacks type-check but refuse.\n51|- TEMPORAL FIXTURE: `good_prechange` now points at a checkpoint head before\n52|  `profile.changed` and resumes with the creation pair yolo/null. The distinct\n53|  `good_divergent` fixture preserves a losing-lease profile-change blob outside\n54|  the authoritative index while admitting the winning standard/changed pair.\n55|  Both remain driven through BuildPlan, fresh/old-plan Revalidate,\n56|  AuthoritativeStatus, and AuthoritativeList.\n57|- MUTANTS: the final local harness reports 65/65 applied N/B plants killed\n58|  (62 narrowing, 3 ordering), including the new\n59|  `N-census-unknown-callback`. Controls are separate: before/after green,\n60|  harmless-comment SURVIVED, not-applied, and compile/harness-failure. No\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
